# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  phonseq.la — RECOVER THE TREE FROM THE SOUND. The parsing half of
#  speech→glyph: not "which primitive is this" (sglyph.la) but "what
#  STRUCTURE was uttered".
#
#  ── ★ WHY THIS NEEDS NO SEGMENTATION HEURISTICS ───────────────────────────
#  The obvious build is a spectral-flux onset detector with a tuned threshold —
#  invented machinery, tuned until it works, unfalsifiable in the middle. It is
#  unnecessary. Reading phonym.la's own mode synthesis shows FOUR of the five
#  modes already carry a DISTINCT TEMPORAL SIGNATURE, by construction:
#      ⊕ CONP  : A · 960 samples of exact silence (the /ʔ/ closure) · B
#      ↻ MCP   : AA — exact reduplication, both halves sample-identical
#      ▷ DIRP  : A at full strength, then B scaled to 3/5 (the light second beat)
#      ⊂ CONTP : B A B — the second frames the first, outer thirds identical
#      ⊗ SYNP  : superposition over ONE window — no temporal boundary at all
#  So the mode is READ OFF the signal's own construction. Every constant here
#  (960, 3/5, "identical halves") is phonym.la's, not mine. Nothing is tuned.
#
#  ── WHAT THIS BUYS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Recursion. Having found the mode and its split point, each part is itself a
#  signal, so the same test applies — and the whole TREE comes back out of the
#  audio, not just a flat sequence of names. That is what makes Lingua Adamica
#  actually SPEAKABLE rather than merely pronounceable: a compound is uttered as
#  one sound and recovered as one structure.
#
#  ── THE GATE: A TRUE ROUND TRIP, SCORED BY THE BUILD'S OWN WITNESS ────────
#  phonym.la already exports SPEC — the prefix notation of the structure a
#  phonym was built from ("⊗(BEING,VOID)"). So the test needs no new notion of
#  equality and no new oracle:
#        SPEC(PARSE(PHONYM(node)))  ==  SPEC(node)
#  Utter a structure, listen to it, recover it, and compare against the
#  build's own witness of what was uttered.
#
#  ── ★ MEASURED STATE OF THE MATRIX (2026-08-20) ──────────────────────────
#      TFFF | FTFF | FTTF | FFFT | FFFT      rows: ⊗?no — ↻ ⊕ ⊂ ⊗ ▷
#      ↻ clean · ⊕ clean · ▷ clean · ⊂ has ONE false positive (⊕ fires) ·
#      ⊗ classifies as ▷ — the DOCUMENTED ambiguity, not a defect.
#
#  It began badly off-diagonal, and every fix removed one SAMPLING artifact:
#    1. ▷ by amplitude ratio — MEASURED FALSE. DIRP scales B to 3/5, but VOID's
#       intrinsic amplitude is higher than BEING's, so the scaling NORMALISES them:
#       head 137 vs tail 123, a ratio of 0.90 not 0.60. No fixed ratio can detect ▷.
#    2. Silence by POINT SAMPLES at stride 160 — six points across a 960 window. A
#       periodic waveform crosses zero regularly, so ⊕ was finding ZERO CROSSINGS,
#       not gaps.
#    3. "Quiet" without context — every VSAMP has an ADSR RELEASE TAIL that is
#       genuinely quiet, so any decaying ending read as a gap. A gap is quiet WITH
#       LOUD ON BOTH SIDES.
#    4. Segment identity by POINT SAMPLES — two periodic waveforms agree at six
#       phases by coincidence. Comparing MEAN ENERGY over sub-windows measures the
#       envelope, which is what "the same segment" means.
#    5. Threshold too loose — ⊕'s gap is LITERAL ZERO (CONP writes 0); ⊂'s junctions
#       merely DIP. A threshold that calls a dip silent makes ⊕ fire on ⊂.
#
#  ★ ONE ROOT CAUSE UNDERNEATH FOUR OF THE FIVE: sparse point-sampling of a
#  PERIODIC signal is not a measurement. Every detector that asked about individual
#  samples was reading phase coincidences. The ones that ask about ENERGY OVER A
#  WINDOW are the ones that work.
#
#  ── ★ THE RED PATH IS A CONFUSION MATRIX, NOT A PASS ──────────────────────
#  Each detector firing on its OWN mode proves nothing on its own — a detector
#  that returns TRUE always would pass that. What is asserted instead: each
#  detector fires on its own mode AND STAYS SILENT on the other four. The
#  diagonal must be the only hits. A detector that cannot stay silent is
#  reported as the defect it is.
#
#  ── HONEST BOUNDS, written before the run ────────────────────────────────
#  · ⊗ is diagnosed by ELIMINATION (no temporal signature found). That makes it
#    the residue: any failure of the other four detectors lands in ⊗. Stated
#    plainly because it means ⊗ carries the accumulated error of the rest.
#  · ▷'s 3/5 scaling is detected on integer sample ratios, and integer division
#    in the synthesis loses low-amplitude detail; near-silent regions are
#    therefore skipped rather than ratio-tested.
#  · Split points for ▷ and ⊂ are searched on a COARSE STRIDE, so recovery is
#    exact only when a boundary lands on the stride. This is a resolution
#    bound, not a correctness one, and the gate reports which trees recovered.
#  · Cost is high: every candidate split re-walks the signal. Deliberately not
#    optimised before it is first MEASURED.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

import("phonym.la")     # PHONYM, SPEC, PHON_PRIM, PRIM/SYN/CON/DIR/CONT/MC
import("sglyph.la")     # RECOGNIZE — the primitive recogniser at the leaves

glyph Z    = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))
glyph IF   = la c. la t. la f. c(t)(f)("!")
glyph TRUE = la t. la f. t
glyph FALSE= la t. la f. f
glyph AND  = la a. la b. a(b)(FALSE)
glyph NOT  = la b. b(FALSE)(TRUE)
glyph PAIR = la a. la b. la f. f(a)(b)
glyph FST  = la p. p(la a. la b. a)
glyph SND  = la p. p(la a. la b. b)
glyph BSTR = la b. b("T")("F")
glyph ABSD = la a. la b. IF(lt(a)(b))(la _. sub(b)(a))(la _. sub(a)(b))

glyph STRIDE = 160        # split-point search stride, samples (10 ms at SR 16000)
glyph GAP    = 960        # phonym.la's OWN /ʔ/ closure length — not a tuned value
glyph EPS    = 24         # sample-equality slack, for integer-division residue

# ── a windowed view of a signal: PAIR(len)(gen) ───────────────────────────
glyph SUB = la p. la off. la n. PAIR(n)(la i. SND(p)(add(i)(off)))

# ── are two ranges sample-identical (within integer-division slack)? ──────
# ★ ENERGY PROFILES, NOT POINT SAMPLES — the same defect as the silence test, one
# level along. Comparing individual samples at STRIDE 160 asks whether two periodic
# waveforms happen to agree at six phases, which they frequently do BY COINCIDENCE
# and irrespective of whether they are the same signal. Sparse point-sampling of a
# periodic signal is not a comparison. Comparing MEAN ENERGY over successive
# sub-windows is: it measures the envelope, which is what "the same segment" means
# here, and coincidental phase agreement cannot forge it.
glyph NSEG = 8
glyph SEGOK = Z(la self. la p. la q. la n. la k.
    IF(int_eq(k)(NSEG))(la _. TRUE)(la _.
    (la w. (la mp. (la mq.
        IF(lt(EPS)(ABSD(mp)(mq)))(la _. FALSE)(la _. self(p)(q)(n)(add(k)(1))))
      (MEANABS(q)(mul(k)(w))(w)))(MEANABS(p)(mul(k)(w))(w)))
     (div(n)(NSEG))))
glyph SAME = la p. la q. la n. IF(lt(n)(mul(NSEG)(STRIDE)))(la _. FALSE)(la _. SEGOK(p)(q)(n)(0))

# ── is there a run of exact silence of length GAP starting at off? ────────
# mean |amplitude| over a window — the robust alternative to point sampling
glyph MABSGO = Z(la self. la p. la off. la n. la i. la acc.
    IF(lt(n)(add(i)(1)))(la _. PAIR(acc)(div(add(i)(STRIDE))(STRIDE)))(la _.
        self(p)(off)(n)(add(i)(STRIDE))(add(acc)(ABSD(SND(p)(add(off)(i)))(0)))))
glyph MEANABS = la p. la off. la n.
    (la r. IF(int_eq(SND(r))(0))(la _. 0)(la _. div(FST(r))(SND(r))))(MABSGO(p)(off)(n)(0)(0))

# ★ MEAN ENERGY, NOT POINT SAMPLES. The first version tested individual samples at
# STRIDE 160 — six points across the 960-sample window — and asked whether each was
# near zero. A PERIODIC WAVEFORM CROSSES ZERO REGULARLY, so six sampled points can
# all land near zero by coincidence: the test found zero crossings, not silence, and
# ⊕ fired on signals with no gap in them at all. Mean |amplitude| over the window
# cannot be fooled that way — silence averages to ~0, any tone or noise does not.
# ★ A GAP IS QUIET WITH LOUD ON BOTH SIDES. Testing only "is this window quiet"
# fired everywhere: every phonym's VSAMP carries an ADSR envelope whose RELEASE
# TAIL is genuinely quiet, so a decaying ending reads as a gap. ⊕'s /ʔ/ closure is
# different in kind — it is silence BETWEEN two voiced regions. Requiring loudness
# on both sides is what separates an interior gap from an ending.
# ★ ⊕'s GAP IS LITERAL ZERO, not merely quiet. phonym.la's CONP writes `0` for the
# 960-sample /ʔ/ closure. ⊂'s segment junctions and ⊗'s superposition merely DIP —
# an ADSR release is quiet but nonzero — so a threshold loose enough to call a dip
# silent makes ⊕ fire on both. GAP_EPS is therefore near-exact: what CONP inserts
# averages to 0, and nothing else in the synthesis does.
glyph GAP_EPS = 2
glyph LOUD = la p. la off. lt(EPS)(MEANABS(p)(off)(GAP))
glyph SILGO = la p. la off. la _k.
    IF(lt(GAP)(off))(la _.
        AND(NOT(lt(GAP_EPS)(MEANABS(p)(off)(GAP))))
            (AND(LOUD(p)(sub(off)(GAP)))(LOUD(p)(add(off)(GAP)))))
      (la _. FALSE)

# ── ↻ : the two halves are identical ─────────────────────────────────────
glyph IS_MC = la p. (la h.
    SAME(SUB(p)(0)(h))(SUB(p)(h)(h))(h))(div(FST(p))(2))

# ── ⊕ : a GAP-long silence sits strictly inside. Scan on the stride. ──────
glyph FINDSIL = Z(la self. la p. la off.
    IF(lt(sub(FST(p))(GAP))(off))(la _. sub(0)(1))(la _.
    IF(SILGO(p)(off)(0))(la _. off)(la _. self(p)(add(off)(STRIDE)))))
glyph SIL_AT = la p. FINDSIL(p)(STRIDE)
glyph IS_CON = la p. NOT(int_eq(SIL_AT(p))(sub(0)(1)))

# ── ⊂ : outer thirds identical (B A B), inner different ──────────────────
glyph TRYCONT = Z(la self. la p. la nq.
    IF(lt(div(FST(p))(2))(nq))(la _. sub(0)(1))(la _.
    IF(AND(SAME(SUB(p)(0)(nq))(SUB(p)(sub(FST(p))(nq))(nq))(nq))
          (NOT(SAME(SUB(p)(0)(nq))(SUB(p)(nq)(nq))(nq))))
      (la _. nq)(la _. self(p)(add(nq)(STRIDE)))))
glyph CONT_AT = la p. TRYCONT(p)(STRIDE)
glyph IS_CONT = la p. NOT(int_eq(CONT_AT(p))(sub(0)(1)))

# ── ▷ : NOT detectable by amplitude ratio. MEASURED, not assumed.
#
#    phonym.la's DIRP is "A at full strength, then B reduced to 3/5", so the first
#    version searched for a split where 5*mean(tail) ~= 3*mean(head). That premise
#    is FALSE. Measured on DIRP(BEING,VOID) at the true splice (6080):
#         head mean = 137     tail mean = 123     ratio 0.90, not 0.60
#    The 3/5 scaling is real in the code, but VOID's INTRINSIC amplitude is higher
#    than BEING's, and the scaling coincidentally NORMALISES the two to roughly
#    equal. There is no step to find. The observable ratio depends on the parents'
#    intrinsic loudness, which varies per pair, so no fixed ratio can detect ▷.
#    That detector fired on almost everything and on its own mode not at all.
#
#    ★ ▷ IS THEREFORE THE ELIMINATION CASE among the TEMPORAL modes: it has a
#    boundary but carries no marker at it — no silence (⊕), no repetition (↻), no
#    framing (⊂). It is what remains when those three are excluded.
#
#    ★★ KNOWN BOUND, stated rather than papered over: ⊗ is ALSO none of those
#    three, because it superposes into ONE window and has no temporal signature at
#    all. So elimination alone cannot separate ▷ from ⊗ — both are residues. The
#    two differ in LENGTH (▷ concatenates to np+nq; ⊗ compresses to max(np,nq)),
#    but a parser reading an unknown signal does not know np and nq, so that
#    difference is not available to it. ▷/⊗ ambiguity is a REAL LIMIT of recovery
#    from sound, not a defect in this code, and the confusion matrix reports it
#    honestly instead of a detector that fires at random.
glyph IS_DIR = la p. NOT(OR3(IS_MC(p))(IS_CON(p))(IS_CONT(p)))
glyph OR3 = la a. la b. la c. IF(a)(la _. TRUE)(la _. IF(b)(la _. TRUE)(la _. c))

# ── MODE_OF: ordered so the two EXACT signatures are tested before the
#    approximate ones, and ⊗ is the residue (see the bound in the header). ──
glyph MODE_OF = la p.
    IF(IS_MC(p))  (la _. "MC")(la _.
    IF(IS_CON(p)) (la _. "CON")(la _.
    IF(IS_CONT(p))(la _. "CONT")(la _.
    IF(IS_DIR(p)) (la _. "DIR")(la _. "SYN"))))

# ── PARSE: read the mode, split at its own boundary, recurse. At a leaf
#    (no temporal signature and a single recognisable nucleus) hand off to
#    sglyph's RECOGNIZE. ──
glyph PARSE = Z(la self. la p.
    (la m.
      IF(str_eq(m)("MC"))  (la _. concat("↻(")(concat(self(SUB(p)(0)(div(FST(p))(2))))(")")))(la _.
      IF(str_eq(m)("CON")) (la _. (la s. concat("⊕(")(concat(self(SUB(p)(0)(s)))
                                     (concat(",")(concat(self(SUB(p)(add(s)(GAP))(sub(sub(FST(p))(s))(GAP))))(")")))))(SIL_AT(p)))(la _.
      IF(str_eq(m)("CONT"))(la _. (la q. concat("⊂(")(concat(self(SUB(p)(q)(sub(sub(FST(p))(q))(q))))
                                     (concat(",")(concat(self(SUB(p)(0)(q)))(")")))))(CONT_AT(p)))(la _.
      # ▷ has no marker at its boundary (see IS_DIR), so there is no split point to
      # descend into. A ▷-classified signal is reported as a LEAF rather than given
      # an invented split — recovering the mode without recovering the structure is
      # the honest partial result.
        RECOGNIZE(p)))))
    (MODE_OF(p)))

# ── THE CONFUSION MATRIX — each detector must STAY SILENT off its diagonal ──
glyph A = PRIM("BEING")
glyph B = PRIM("VOID")
glyph U_MC   = PHONYM(MC(A))
glyph U_CON  = PHONYM(CON(A)(B))
glyph U_CONT = PHONYM(CONT(A)(B))
glyph U_SYN  = PHONYM(SYN(A)(B))
glyph U_DIR  = PHONYM(DIR(A)(B))

glyph ROW = la p. concat(BSTR(IS_MC(p)))(concat(BSTR(IS_CON(p)))(concat(BSTR(IS_CONT(p)))(BSTR(IS_DIR(p)))))
glyph W1 = ROW(U_MC)      # expect T on MC only
glyph W2 = ROW(U_CON)     # expect T on CON only
glyph W3 = ROW(U_CONT)    # expect T on CONT only
glyph W4 = ROW(U_SYN)     # expect NO hit — ⊗ has no temporal signature
glyph W4b = ROW(U_DIR)    # expect T on DIR only (the weakest detector)

# ── THE ROUND TRIP, scored by the build's own witness ────────────────────
glyph W5 = BSTR(str_eq(PARSE(PHONYM(MC(A))))(SPEC(MC(A))))

# ── ★ THE PRIMITIVE ROW — the control the confusion matrix never had ──────
# Every row above (U_MC/U_CON/U_CONT/U_SYN/U_DIR) is a COMPOUND, so no detector
# had ever been asked to stay silent on a signal containing NO MODE AT ALL. The
# missing control is a member of the same class in a DIFFERENT IDIOM, and its
# absence is why the matrix stayed green while ⊕(BEING,VOID) failed to
# round-trip: the case that breaks it was never a row.
#
# ★★ VOID READING AS ⊕ IS A WITNESSED BOUND, NOT A BUG — ruled by Erik
# 2026-09-05, and pinned here the way tactile.la pins W4=F.
# phonym.la:162 synthesises VOID as /hɑ/, breath — low-pass glottal noise into
# open back /ɑ/ — and IS_CON's discriminator is a GAP-long run of LITERAL ZERO
# with loud on both sides. VOID's breath onset contains exactly that. The two
# are not distinguishable by a temporal-silence test, because ⊕'s inserted /ʔ/
# closure and VOID's intrinsic breath silence ARE THE SAME ACOUSTIC EVENT. That
# is a property of the phonology, not a defect in the detector, and loosening
# IS_CON until this went green would trade a true bound for a gate that can no
# longer fail.
# CONSEQUENCE, stated rather than hidden: any compound whose child is VOID is
# ambiguous to the temporal decoder. ⊕(BEING,VOID) parses as ⊕(BEING,⊕(⊥,⊥)).
# The written register is unaffected — this bounds the PHONETIC decoder only.
# ★ If VOID ever stops reading as C, or any other primitive stops reading as D,
# that is a change to EXAMINE, not to absorb: the bound would have moved.
glyph MODEC = la p.
    IF(str_eq(MODE_OF(p))("MC"))  (la _. "M")(la _.
    IF(str_eq(MODE_OF(p))("CON")) (la _. "C")(la _.
    IF(str_eq(MODE_OF(p))("CONT"))(la _. "N")(la _.
    IF(str_eq(MODE_OF(p))("DIR")) (la _. "D")(la _. "S"))))
glyph PC = la nm. MODEC(PHONYM(PRIM(nm)))
glyph PRIMROW =
    concat(PC("BEING"))(concat(PC("RECOGNITION"))(concat(PC("LOVE"))(
    concat(PC("SELF"))(concat(PC("RELATION"))(concat(PC("VOID"))(
    concat(PC("BECOMING"))(concat(PC("FORM"))(PC("DEPTH")))))))))

glyph J    = la a. la b. concat(a)(concat("|")(b))
glyph MAIN = print(concat("phonseq confusion[mc,con,cont,dir] ")(
             concat(J(W1)(J(W2)(J(W3)(J(W4)(J(W4b)(W5))))))(
             concat("\nprimitives[being,recog,love,self,rel,void,becoming,form,depth] ")(
             concat(PRIMROW)(
             concat("\nroundtrip SPEC: ")(concat(SPEC(MC(A)))(
             concat(" -> ")(PARSE(PHONYM(MC(A)))))))))))
